A. Camera pose from the board puck alone (0.15 px feature noise, 1-sigma)
   H (mm)   x,y (um)     height (um)   tilt (mdeg)   roll about the axis (mdeg)   mm per pixel at the plate
     150     16.4/  16.2        3.3       5.91/ 5.97        1.27                    0.100
     300    124.1/ 123.3       13.3      23.35/23.50        2.56                    0.200
     450    381.3/ 380.2       30.1      48.30/48.43        3.85                    0.300
   (a flat board at one pose cannot separate focal length from height; f is assumed known here.  Section D of the idea file says how f is found.)

B. Seat depth d of a tube from its rim and ports (0.15 px), pose free vs pose given by the board.  1-sigma in mm
   H (mm)   pose free   pose from board   with drift since calibration 0.05 mm & 0.005 deg
     150     0.029       0.006             0.025
     300     0.115       0.024             0.051
     450     0.259       0.054             0.073

C. Predicted corner position at the station (mm 1-sigma along the image x and y axes) from the two routes
   H (mm)   tube alone (pose free, d free)    board pose + tube (drift as above)
     150    0.012 / 0.003                         0.011 / 0.003
     300    0.025 / 0.006                         0.011 / 0.005
     450    0.038 / 0.009                         0.012 / 0.007

D. Seat repeatability of a puck (10 um per landing at the balls, ball circle 172 mm): lateral 20 um and vertical 4 um at the weld circle [swap_budget.py]
   so a calibration made on the board puck carries an extra 20 um lateral / 4 um vertical when read on any puck, and nothing else.
